[2026-01-30T00:26:44.578Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01TVW1SvAe3vEMY2a2dJKiBN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Report Interactive Features - Pragmatic Integrator Complete ✓\n\n**Scan ID:** `8c9bb2cf-2df4-49d6-8404-176d5f4d25d9`\n\n**5 Ideas Created:**\n\n1. **Consolidate FocusMode and SpeedReader Into Single Component** - Both duplicate overlay setup, keyboard handling, and exit mechanics. Merge into one ReadingMode component with mode toggle, reducing ~100 lines and creating one mental model.\n\n2. **Remove Redundant SpotlightText From FocusMode** - SpotlightText's sentence-level hover highlighting competes with FocusMode's spotlight. Delete the 45-line component that adds complexity without clear benefit.\n\n3. **Connect KeyPointsPanel Actions To Actual Navigation** - The onPointClick callback just toggles expansion. Wire it to actually navigate to related findings/sources. Complete the broken user journey from \"see key point\" to \"investigate it.\"\n\n4. **Hardcode Default WPM in SpeedReader** - The wordsPerMinute prop defaults to 300 and is never overridden. Remove the prop and hardcode the initial value - the runtime slider still allows adjustment. Eliminate unused configuration surface.\n\n5. **Add Unified Reading Mode Launcher** - Instead of separate entry points for each reading feature, create a single keyboard shortcut (R) that presents a mode choice. One entry point reduces cognitive load and improves discoverability.\n\n**Key Observation:** These features are individually useful but disconnected. KeyPointsPanel shows insights but can't act on them. FocusMode and SpeedReader share mechanics but are separate components. The pragmatic path is to consolidate the reading modes and connect KeyPointsPanel to navigation - transforming isolated widgets into an integrated reading experience."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cac